   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Hi.</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">I just decided to validate my RQTL results with<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\"> QTL IciMapping software to be specific;</span> <span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:11pt\">inclusive composite interval mapping (ICIM-ADD) and interval mapping (</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:11pt\">IM-ADD).</span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:11pt\">The good news is that there are several similar QTLs detected with the three methods. However, when it comes to the additive effects, RQTL gives me an opposite additive effect</span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:11pt\"> to that determined by </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:16px\">IciMapping. Have you ever come across such a question or observation?</span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:16px\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">This is just one trait, but that&#39;s what I am observing with all other traits.</span></font></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Thanks</span></font></div></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:16px\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/pro